            10. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying a Robot Rated Too Small</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A robot rated for a 30-foot pool will not clean a 45-foot pool properly, and a cordless robot rated at exactly your pool's area may run out of battery before it finishes. Measure the pool and choose a rating with margin.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the Warranty Terms</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Warranties range from one to three years and can differ by region for the same model name. Motor and power supply repairs are expensive, so read the warranty for your exact model before buying.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Not Cleaning the Filter After Each Cycle</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A clogged filter cuts suction and makes the motor work harder. Clean the filter or basket after every run, and use a coarse filter in leafy seasons if your robot offers one.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Leaving the Robot in the Pool Full-Time</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Constant chlorine and sun exposure ages seals and plastics. Most makers expect you to remove the robot after cycles and when shocking the pool.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Trusting Runtime Claims Without Margin</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Cordless runtime claims are often maximums in the most economical mode. Independent reviews have found shorter real-world cycles. Choose a robot whose runtime comfortably exceeds what your pool needs.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

