          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most inground pools, the <strong class="text-white">Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus with Wi-Fi</strong> is the robot to buy: corded reliability, a 60-foot cable and a multi-year warranty on its main listings. The <strong class="text-white">Dolphin Sigma</strong> adds waterline cleaning and three years of cover, and the <strong class="text-white">Polaris 9550 Sport</strong> handles pools up to 60 feet.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you would never lay out a cable, the <strong class="text-white">Aiper Scuba S1</strong> is the easiest cordless robot for small and mid-size pools, but give any cordless runtime claim plenty of margin. Whatever you buy, clean the filter after every cycle and check the warranty for your exact model.
          </p>
